                activity="Cycling"
                activity_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:15.419-07:00"
                adventureType="Overnight Trip"
                adventureType_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:15.418-07:00"
                description="&lt;p>Southern Utah is a landscape of red cliffs, natural arches and roads with almost no traffic. We cross it by road bike over five days, riding between 60 and 110 kilometres a day with a support van that carries the bags, the water and anyone who has had enough. The climbs are long and the air is thin and dry, so this is a trip for fit, experienced riders.&lt;/p>"
                description_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                description_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:15.417-07:00"
                difficulty="Advanced"
                difficulty_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:15.419-07:00"
                gearList="&lt;ul>&#xa;&lt;li>Your own road bike, or one of ours on request&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Helmet, cycling clothes for hot days and a wind jacket for the descents&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;li>Walking shoes for the afternoon on foot&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ul>"
                gearList_x0040_ContentType="text/html"
                gearList_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2020-10-19T11:53:15.421-07:00"
                groupSize="{Long}14"
                groupSize_x0040_LastModified="{Date}2022-05-26T11:43:22.372-07:00"
                itinerary="&lt;h2>Day 1: Into the canyons&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>A two-hour transfer from the airport to the lodge, bike fitting and a short ride at the end of the afternoon to loosen the legs. Dinner and a briefing on the days ahead.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h2>Days 2 to 4: Three stages&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>Each day follows the same pattern: an early start while it is cool, a long climb to a plateau, lunch from the van at a viewpoint and a descent to the next lodge. Day three is the hardest, with 1,800 metres of climbing, and ends at a rim where the sunset is worth the effort. On day four there is time for a walk among the rock formations on foot.&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;h2>Day 5: The last descent&lt;/h2>&#xa;&lt;p>A morning ride of 60 kilometres, mostly downhill, lunch together and transfers back to the airport.&lt;/p>"
